<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4026.18">
  <DUT Name="ST_HmiLogFileCfg" Id="{1bef92bc-d60e-5b9e-951b-0860e559b6d4}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
   Operator-tunable config for the durable CSV log. Phase 1 of
   docs/plans/log-csv-file.md.

   Instanced as GVL_HmiPersistent.stLogFileCfg, i.e. VAR_GLOBAL PERSISTENT.
   Read the PERSISTENT DATA section of CLAUDE.md before adding a field here:
   PERSISTENT declares a durable storage CLASS, not an automatic save, and it is
   FB_PersistentAutoSave that actually flushes it ~2 s after edits stop. A new
   field is invisible to that FB until it is added to the shadow compare.

   COLD-BOOT DECISION, which CLAUDE.md requires for every new persistent field:
   NOTHING HERE IS CLEARED in MAIN's cold-boot block. Every field is operator or
   commissioning config, so surviving a power cycle is the entire point. Contrast
   the machine-state fields, where a persisted value can move pistons on power-up
   and which is why that block exists at all. Nothing here can start a motion.

   PER-FIELD COMMENTS IN THIS STRUCT MUST STAY SHORT -- put the prose in
   docs/plans/log-csv-file.md instead. This block, being the TYPE's comment, is
   free; a MEMBER's comment is not. TwinCAT ships a symbol's declaration comment
   inside its ADS symbol-info reply, and pyads' receive buffer is 798 bytes.
   sDir's original ~2.8 kB comment produced a 2967-byte reply, which fails
   symbol-info resolution -- and because read_list_by_name resolves every name
   in a sum-up up front, that took the field out of FlowerPyHmi's batched poll
   and onto an individual round trip: +88 ms on a 100 ms cycle, /events 3.3 Hz
   -> 2.62 Hz, measured against this panel 2026-08-12. FlowerPyHmi caps how many
   such symbols it will carry (5), and three others in this project are already
   spending that budget: GVL_HMI.bAutoMode (1400 B),
   GVL_Robot.stParams.nStateOut (991 B) and GVL_Robot.stRobot.nConnectFails
   (817 B).

   So the rule is not "write less"; it is "write it where an ADS client will not
   have to download it 10 times a second."
*)
TYPE ST_HmiLogFileCfg :
STRUCT
    // DEFAULT OFF, deliberately. The panel boots from Compact Flash and CF has
    // a finite erase budget -- the reason FB_PersistentAutoSave debounces its
    // own writes rather than saving on every keystroke. A machine that never
    // needs the file log should never spend flash on it, so writing to the card
    // is an explicit opt-in rather than something inherited from a download.
    bEnabled      : BOOL := FALSE;

    // Directory, WITH a trailing backslash; the writer appends the filename.
    // MUST stay under '\Hard Disk\': '\Temp\' and the device root are the WinCE
    // RAM object store and do not survive a restart. Never fall back to them.
    // Reasoning, measurements and the two rules: docs/plans/log-csv-file.md.
    // KEEP SHORT -- this comment ships in the ADS symbol-info reply (798 B cap);
    // oversized, it drops sDir out of FlowerPyHmi's batched poll. See below.
    sDir          : STRING(80) := '\Hard Disk\Logs\';

    // Roll to a new file part within the day if one file passes this. A guard
    // against a fault storm producing a single unwieldy file, not the primary
    // rotation trigger -- that is the date.
    uiMaxFileKB   : UDINT := 512;

    // Total ceiling for the directory. Phase 3 deletes oldest-first until the
    // sum is under this. 16 MB of INFO-level CSV is months of normal running.
    uiMaxTotalMB  : UDINT := 16;

    // Buffer flush interval. THE FLASH-WEAR CONTROL: entries accumulate in RAM
    // and reach the card once per interval, so a busy second costs one write
    // rather than dozens. Do not "improve" this into a write-per-entry -- that
    // is the change this comment exists to prevent.
    uiFlushSec    : UDINT := 10;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
